#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:5
#: f4aeb02849e3451a9c66349edee5c534
msgid "DIY Camera Trigger using Relay"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:10
#: 426a684c921a440eab4be919a7c0ca04
msgid "This guide is intended to help you modify a remote shutter release cable for use with ArduPilot autopilots and setup the flight controller for triggering the camera. This method eliminates the need (and costs) for 3\\ :sup:`rd` party triggering devices. In this specific example, we will use a Sony Alpha 6000 (A6000) camera. This procedure may work with other cameras however for this specific example, we will use a Sony Alpha A6000 (A6000)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:19
#: 49d3960218534ea8a0333e0f2cabc43c
msgid "Items Required"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:21
#: fbf4c1f6fb9c46cbb58640766afd9dae
msgid "Sony A6000 (or other camera with wire shutter release)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:22
#: fbe635080264417bb65ff8d5fd5cf380
msgid "ArduPilot compatible autopilot with a free GPIO pin to be used as a relay pin. See :ref:`common-gpios` for more information"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:23
#: df3c9e8de76642eca38646e4478715f4
msgid "Remote Shutter Release Cable (`see here for an affordable solution <https://www.amazon.com/SHOOT-DSC-RX100M3-DSC-RX100M20-DSC-RX100II-DSC-RX100III/dp/B00ME7N6P8/ref=sr_1_1?ie=UTF8&qid=1496578319&sr=8-1&keywords=Sony+A6000+Shutter+Release+Cable>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:24
#: e7a7a709277d48789bb8d55f279873eb
msgid "Servo Pins (`link <https://www.digikey.com/products/en?keywords=952-2157-1-ND>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:25
#: b55e61fae5dc41f69a6352db7fb51649
msgid "Servo Pin Crimper (`link <https://www.servocity.com/pin-crimpers>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:26
#: e764e5a3bb5a4152a2ab636ffc21ce92
msgid "Wire Stripper or Razor Blade"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:27
#: fe78ac6ecc4d466ba7b26050f10c2db8
msgid "Laptop with Mission Planner Installed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:29
#: 6b461951cb4242a582aa5a25daeb3abe
msgid "**Step 1:** Preparing the Remote Shutter Release Cable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:31
#: fed0ec95da654359afed8728b24fa6df
msgid "Trim the Remote Shutter Release Cable to the desired cable length"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:36
#: f1c4f711ae244acd98cf371cf028983b
msgid "Strip off approximately 2-3cm of the black sleeve making sure not to damage the 3 wires contained within the sleeve."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:41
#: 0d488c81186d4e879ba589ddf6e378ac
msgid "Remove approximately 3mm of the sleeves off of each of the three wires. You will need to make sure that there is enough of the sleeve removed that when the servo pin is crimped to the wire that there is contact between the pin and the exposed wire."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:46
#: a2b4c577ba924615b32451c32d7d0665
msgid "The three wires have the following functions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:48
#: 75030c6ec2df4de492df2c2a084fb91f
msgid "RED: SHUTTER"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:49
#: 3a266fdd45ca47de8009d8a91f9a0e7d
msgid "YELLOW: GROUND"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:50
#: b9e8d8ea643944bbbd65ce64ab80cda9
msgid "WHITE: FOCUS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:52
#: 7336906461e04ecb908cab7aeefdd395
msgid "**NOTE:** Your wire coloring may differ from this example. You can identify which functions are controlled by each cable by connecting the cable to your camera, powering it on and then shorting the cables in pairs to identify which pair does what. For example, if you have a GREEN, BLUE and BLACK set of wires and shorting BLUE and BLACK results in the camera focusing, and then you short the GREEN AND BLUE wires and nothing happens but shorting the GREEN AND BLACK results in the camera exposing, then you know that the BLACK wire is ground, GREEN is shutter and BLUE is focus."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:62
#: eedf608c2b8d4e9e94fef6c4db4439f6
msgid "Twist the exposed ends of the FOCUS and GROUND wires together then crimp a servo connector to the pair as well as to the exposed end of the SHUTTER wire"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:70
#: 1f49f688fa984ceb9cd9f93cebd307bb
msgid "TIP: The Servo Pin has two sets of tabs which after crimping will fold on each other and secure the wire. To make life a little easier, use a small pair of needle nose pliers to press the pair of tabs on the end of the servo pin tightly against the wires. This will prevent the wires from coming out of the servo pin while trying to crimp them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:82
#: 3b5103567fd94c7f9d9a86e403d0ca29
msgid "Insert the Servo Pins into a Servo connector, one pin on each side of the middle slot of the servo connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:87
#: e705860e3e9143bca732a4f1e47ce1e1
msgid "The cable is now ready for connection to your Pixhawk Controller. Note that the Shutter Pin (in this case the RED wire) will be on the SIGNAL side of the Auxiliary port while the WHITE/YELLOW wire will be on the GROUND side of the Auxiliary port."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:95
#: a5b3659e308c4bc2adccbdb5a6a1b9e7
msgid "**Step 2:** Setting up your  autopilot to trigger your camera via the Shutter Release Cable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:98
#: d593955648ff44b39f196cdfaf618f1c
msgid "Connect to your Autopilot via Mission Planner either through direct USB connection or wireless telemetry link."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:100
#: 9f9e2f07fdc84b368e0564af364c6767
msgid "Connect your modified shutter release cable to a free GPIO capable pin on the autopilot making sure to maintain the correct orientation for polarity. For example, by default on the Pixhawk, AUX5 or AUX6 is configured to be a GPIO and can be used as a Relay output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:102
#: 1afbcdaafae54d2198be56516ebc454c
msgid "Connect the shutter release cable to your camera and power the camera on"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:107
#: 832778bb908b4fd3af92faf82868a80f
msgid "Since we have shorted the FOCUS and GROUND wires, the camera should automatically pull focus. As of now, I have not found a way to connect the SHUTTER, FOCUS and GROUND wires individually to the autopilot and have the autopilot pull the camera focus and trigger the camera in sequence. To get around this, the camera settings are set so that the camera has the following features activated:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:114
#: ca481a7dd9b242bf9cafdbd7eaca6fc4
msgid "Pre-Shutter Focus"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:116
#: 189e8ef25805497a940a0d5530ab72b8
msgid "Continuous Auto-Focus"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:118
#: 82495a3f676e41788cd1bab8cfa18c25
msgid "In Mission Planner, navigate to INITIAL SETUP -> CAMERA GIMBAL and change the SHUTTER drop-down menu to “RELAY”"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:123
#: 72498d1497f2470aacbbd5bf9140e229
msgid "NOTE: You can play around with the “Duration” values to increase or decrease the responsiveness of the shutter command. With the Sony A6000, a duration of 1/10\\ :sup:`th` of a Second functions perfectly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:127
#: 40dc6816e87e45fcae88588a14111bb5
msgid "Proceed to the CONFIG/TUNING -> EXTENDED TUNING screen in Mission Planner and change the CH7 OPT to “Camera Trigger”. This will be necessary if you intend to use your remote controls CH7 to trigger the camera in addition to having the autopilot trigger the camera."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:132
#: 1e35b951688a43bb9fe12e9f39b2921a
msgid "As of 4.0 firmware versions, any GPIO can be assigned as the Camera Trigger pin via its ``SERVOx_FUNCTION`` parameter, and any RC channel can be assigned to control that trigger via its ``RCx_OPTION`` parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:135
#: 6700b29098924da78fbfd66763e9f51c
msgid "Navigate to the FULL PARAMETER LIST under the main CONFIG/TUNING tab and locate the ``CAMx_TRIGG_TYPE`` parameter. This parameter must show as 1 for “RELAY”. If it is not set to 1, change this parameter to 1 before proceeding to the next step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:140
#: 0093e47bf4a54747ac9facccc1a12a58
msgid "Scroll down through the parameters until you get to ``RELAYx_PIN`` (for the first relay pin...there can be up to 6) . Here you will want to set the ``RELAY_PIN``  parameter to match the GPIO pin you have connected the shutter release cable to. Since we have connected the cable to AUX6 on a Pixhawk, we need to change the ``RELAYx_PIN``  parameter to “55” (55:Pixhawk AUXOUT6)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:145
#: dc3afec7f941437c86e8c16104be4641
msgid "Now that the required parameters have been changed, click on “WRITE PARAMS”"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:150
#: 7a4af76a0d834aa78686525692ebcf2d
msgid "**Step 3:** Testing the Remote Shutter Cable and Autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:152
#: 5f505897c955452d8b3e6ae294a4645f
msgid "Now that the cable has been modified and connected to the autopilot which has been setup to trigger the camera via relay, let’s test it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:155
#: 3db5a781bc2e412c89d0306504a3a8f8
msgid "Navigate back to the FLIGHT DATA Screen and right click on the map to select “TRIGGER CAMERA NOW”"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:160
#: 696e7e16dddf496fb443464d819fdc31
msgid "Once clicked, you should hear or see the camera expose. If the camera does not expose, check the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:163
#: f97c652b05e04c5bbab72c1f14bcae3c
msgid "Correct Orientation of cables (ie, Shutter Wire is connected to the SIGNAL pin on the correct port of the autopilot and Ground is connected to Ground)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:164
#: cb62b3a114f44026b19f22364e732258
msgid "Camera is On and not in an Error State"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:165
#: 2ee325015bbc4cdbbce0b595ae305408
msgid "Camera lens is not too close to an object which may cause it to be unable to autofocus and expose"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:167
#: 36a5c9a508124f10b764f4c512a7e547
msgid "If you still are not getting the camera to expose and all of the above-mentioned check points are not a problem, then you may want to adjust the Shutter Duration mentioned in Step 2 Part D."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:171
#: 75d9343105494627bb1c5cf8f4e3799b
msgid "If your camera took a picture, congratulations! You are all set to take pictures using the autopilot without needing third party hardware!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-camera-trigger-setup.rst:175
#: 9758d6fd91654720a5cfd566d08ea50f
msgid "Many thanks to Oliver Volkmann and `*www.microaerialprojects.com* <http://www.microaerialprojects.com/>`__ for contributing this page."
msgstr ""
